<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 29-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 29-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 29-day Cetes rate fell in this week's primary auction and demand fell, Banco de Mexico said on Monday.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>29-Day	19.71	    - 52	    19.03     19.99</p>
<p>92-Day	22.08	    + 15	    22.01     22.14</p>
<p>183-Day     23.18	    + 72	    23.01     23.31</p>
<p>337-Day     24.35				24.15     24.46</p>
<p>Last week the 343-day paper was assigned at 23.72 percent.</p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>29-Day	800 million pesos   2.18 bln pesos    2.72</p>
<p>92-Day	800 million pesos   4.65 bln pesos    5.81</p>
<p>183-Day     800 million pesos   4.14 bln pesos    5.17</p>
<p>337-Day     600 million pesos   3.03 bln pesos    5.05</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 4.66 on demand of 13.99 billion pesos compared to 6.34 the week before on demand of 19.02 billion pesos the week before.</p>
<p>Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    29-Day			   28 basis points</p>
<p>    92-Day			    6 basis points</p>
<p>    183-Day			  13 basis points</p>
<p>    337-Day			  11 basis points</p>
<p>((--Dan Trotta, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9507))</p>
